      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, if I am understanding how purgeable resources work, really nothing needs to be done here and it should \"just work\". By that I mean that within this design, a non-shareable resource (like a descriptor set) will not be returned and ref\u0027d if it is currently in use already. Once it\u0027s no longer in use, it is returned to the cache to be reused again and not automatically. Is that correct?\n\nIf so, I will go ahead and abandon this CL and collaborate with Michael with any edge cases we encounter along the way while using purgeable resources this way.",
      "revId": "f8027d632921a2b951e3f13118ae682e893e0d03",
